  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A modulating signal is a square wave, as shown in the figure.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0022_4e45ffcacbb9.png\" style=\"width: 543px; height: 121px;\" /></p><p>If the carrier wave is given as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> volts, the modulation index is:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0022_4e45ffcacbb9.png\" style=\"width: 543px; height: 121px;\" /></p><p>Modulation index &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math>&#39; is related to amplitude of modulation signal &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></math>&#39; and amplitude of carrier wave &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></math>&#39; as:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, from graph&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;and from equation of carrier wave&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>"
  }
